  "title": "The Cupboard Behind the Cupboard",
  "family": "learning",
  "category": "home organization",
  "premise": "A cook wants to find a frequently used lid, but deep stacks hide it behind rarely used pieces. A cutaway separates visible access space from hidden storage and gives the lid a reachable, labeled slot.",
  "hook": "How many things must move before this lid can leave?",
  "visible_action": "A cupboard becomes transparent; ghost paths count obstacles before a vertical divider gives each lid a direct exit.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Storage usefulness depends on retrieval effort as well as total capacity.",
  "gate": "Use a toy cupboard; do not prescribe load limits or physical accessibility from the animation.",
